              "agc_cp",
              "agc"
            ],
            "public_requirement": "A transistor-level AGC amplifier and manual or automatic gain selector must produce agc and select mgc or agc onto gc according to mc.",
            "electrical_reason": "The detector-to-AGC inputs are exclusively AC coupled by Caga and Cagb. At the detector's rectified/averaged DC error output, these capacitors are open, while Ragbp and Ragbn force both AGC input bases to vref13. Consequently the active differential pair and follower establish only a quiescent agc value independent of the detector amplitude; no DC detector-error control path exists to drive automatic gain control. The reported zero AGC gain is consistent with this disconnection. The transmission-gate selector is electrically valid, but it merely selects this nonresponsive agc node in automatic mode."
          }
        ]
      },
