              "Ragbn",
              "XQagp",
              "XQagn",
              "XQagef",
              "XMagef",
              "XMngc",
              "XMpgc2"
            ],
            "nodes": [
              "detp",
              "detn",
              "agc_bp",
              "agc_bn",
              "vref13",
              "agc",
              "gc"
            ],
            "public_requirement": "The required TIA, two RF stages, output buffer, detector, AGC, and selector must form a complete receiver whose finalp and finaln outputs meet the nominal, overload, power, and PAM4 requirements.",
            "electrical_reason": "Although the forward TIA-to-output chain is connected, the required automatic control path is not physically coherent for the detector's averaged output: Caga and Cagb block the detector DC response and Ragbp/Ragbn rebias both AGC inputs to vref13. Thus agc cannot convey detector amplitude to the automatic selector devices XMngc/XMpgc2 and gc, leaving the detector/AGC feedback portion of the claimed complete receiver functionally disconnected."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "summary": "The input TIA/cancellation, two gc-controlled RF stages, active output buffer, and active detector are genuinely implemented and connected. The AGC amplifier lacks a DC path from the rectified detector outputs, so automatic detector-based gain control and therefore the full closed receiver control path are not implemented."
